# CODEOWNERS: who is asked to review a pull request, by path.
#
# How it works: when a pull request touches a path below, GitHub
# automatically requests a review from the owners listed on that line.
# The last matching line wins.
#
# Every owner below is still TBD(team). To activate a line, remove the
# leading "# " and replace the placeholder with a GitHub username, for
# example:   /hardware/   @someones-username
# Several owners can share a line, separated by spaces.
#
# Until at least one line is active this file does nothing, which is fine.

# Schematics, layout, libraries, simulations
# /hardware/                   @TBD-hardware-lead
# /hardware/controller-board/  @TBD-controller-board-owner
# /hardware/fret-board/        @TBD-fret-board-owner

# Firmware
# /firmware/                   @TBD-firmware-lead
# /firmware/bsp/               @TBD-bsp-owner

# Mechanical
# /mechanical/                 @TBD-mechanical-lead

# Requirements, architecture and decisions affect everyone
# /docs/requirements.md        @TBD-team-lead
# /docs/architecture.md        @TBD-team-lead
# /docs/decisions/             @TBD-team-lead

# CI and repository tooling
# /.github/                    @TBD-repo-maintainer
# /tools/                      @TBD-repo-maintainer
